/-
# Generic groups with free small subgroups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 11.75)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.75 (A. Yu. Olshanskii): consider the class
of groups with `n` generators and `m` relators; a subclass is dense if the ratio of the number of
presentations `⟨a₁, …, aₙ | R₁, …, R_m⟩` (`|Rᵢ| = dᵢ`) for groups from this subclass to the number
of all such presentations converges to `1` when `d₁ + ⋯ + d_m` tends to infinity. Prove that for
every `k < m` and for any `n` the subclass of groups all of whose `k`-generator subgroups are free
is dense.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Data.Set.Card
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.CyclicallyReduced
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.IsFreeGroup
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PresentedGroup
public import Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.Pseudo.Defs

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GenericFreeSubgroupsKourovka11Problem75Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.75 (A. Yu.
Olshanskii). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700767 (`KOU-11.75`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Reading. The Notebook writes `n` generators, `m` relators and `k < m`; with `k` at least the number
of generators the whole group would have to be free, which fails generically, and the resolving
paper (by the proposer, whose title reads "subgroups with lesser number of generators are free")
proves the statement for subgroups generated by fewer elements than the number of generators, and
presents it as the answer: its abstract states that in almost every group with `m` generators and
`n` relations any subgroup generated by less than `m` elements is free and that "in particular, this
solves Problem 11.75 from the Kourovka Notebook". The module follows the paper as summarized in
zbMATH Zbl 0877.20021: for `m ≥ 2` generators and `n` relators, presentations are `n`-tuples of
cyclically reduced words (the empty word counts as cyclically reduced, as in Mathlib), `N_d` counts
those of total length `|r₁| + ⋯ + |rₙ| = d`, and the proportion of them whose group has every
subgroup generated by at most `m - 1` elements free tends to `1`. At least one relator is required
(with none there is a single presentation, of length `0`).
-/

/-- The presentations `⟨x₁, …, x_m | r₁, …, r_n⟩` counted by Arzhantseva and Olshanskii: `n`-tuples
of cyclically reduced words in the free group on `m` letters, of total length `d`. -/
def presentations (m n d : ℕ) : Set (Fin n → FreeGroup (Fin m)) :=
  {r | (∀ i, FreeGroup.IsCyclicallyReduced (r i).toWord) ∧ ∑ i, (r i).norm = d}

/-- Every subgroup of `G` generated by fewer than `m` elements is free. -/
def SubgroupsWithFewerGeneratorsFree (m : ℕ) (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∀ s : Finset G, s.card < m → IsFreeGroup (Subgroup.closure (s : Set G))

/-- Kourovka 11.75 (A. Yu. Olshanskii), in the form proved by Arzhantseva and Olshanskii: for
`m ≥ 2` generators and `n ≥ 1` relators, the proportion of presentations of total relator length
`d` whose group has all subgroups generated by fewer than `m` elements free tends to `1` as
`d → ∞`. -/
def fewerGeneratorSubgroupsFreeGeneric : Prop :=
  ∀ m n : ℕ, 2 ≤ m → 1 ≤ n →
    Filter.Tendsto
      (fun d => (({r ∈ presentations m n d |
          SubgroupsWithFewerGeneratorsFree m (PresentedGroup (Set.range r))} : Set _).ncard : ℝ) /
        (presentations m n d).ncard)
      Filter.atTop (nhds 1)

/--
Resolved true: Arzhantseva and Olshanskii prove that for presentations with `m ≥ 2` generators and
`n` cyclically reduced relators of total length `d`, the proportion whose group has all `(m -
1)`-generated subgroups free tends to `1` as `d → ∞`; the Kourovka Archive records 11.75 as proved
by this paper. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory:
The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem
11.75 (A. Yu. Olshanskii); resolution: G. N. Arzhantseva and A. Yu. Olshanskii, The class of groups
all of whose subgroups with lesser number of generators are free is generic, Math. Notes 59 (1996),
no. 4, 350-355 (Mat. Zametki 59 (1996), 489-496), Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.75: This is proved
(Arzhantseva-Olshanskii); paper, abstract ("this solves Problem 11.75 from the Kourovka Notebook")
and main theorem as summarized in zbMATH Zbl 0877.20021 (lim N_d^f / N_d = 1 over presentations with
cyclically reduced relators of total length d), https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02308683.
-/
public theorem_wanted fewerGeneratorSubgroupsFreeGeneric_holds : fewerGeneratorSubgroupsFreeGeneric

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GenericFreeSubgroupsKourovka11Problem75Wanted
